                            <comment id="14553931" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 21 May 2015 09:03:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Should be unmuted for IgniteGridGain Basic Portable configuration as well.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15877697" author="somefire" created="Wed, 22 Feb 2017 07:45:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Don&apos;t forget to unmute test.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15877821" author="somefire" created="Wed, 22 Feb 2017 09:10:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Test fixed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CI tests:&lt;a href=&quot;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests=pull%2F1564%2Fhead&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests=pull%2F1564%2Fhead&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PR: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15935287" author="agura" created="Tue, 21 Mar 2017 20:37:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, this change doesn&apos;t fix the problem at all. The main goal is avoid of &lt;tt&gt;StackOverflowError&lt;/tt&gt; due to a cyclic referencing. So class &lt;tt&gt;GridToStringBuilder&lt;/tt&gt; should be fixed, not test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also your PR contains 95% formatting related changes. Please, don&apos;t do it in a such way anymore. It makes code review to difficult.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15960526" author="somefire" created="Fri, 7 Apr 2017 09:06:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, sorry for formatting, it was a habit to use auto-formating function in IDEA. Ok, I fixed &lt;tt&gt;GridToStringBuilder&lt;/tt&gt;. My solution is to call a similar function for every additional argument as for the main argument. Is it normal?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15974804" author="agura" created="Wed, 19 Apr 2017 14:41:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, to be honest I can&apos;t understand the main idea of this fix. Also I have simple test case that still fails:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;    /**
     * @&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throws&lt;/span&gt; Exception If failed.
     */
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; void testToStringCheckAdvancedRecursionPrevention2() &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throws&lt;/span&gt; Exception {
        Node n1 = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Node();
        Node n2 = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Node();

        n1.next = n2;
        n2.next = n1;

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;.out.println(n1);
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;.out.println(n2);
    }

    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;Node {
        @GridToStringInclude
        Node next;

        @Override &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; toString() {
            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; GridToStringBuilder.toString(Node.class, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;);
        }
    }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15983080" author="somefire" created="Tue, 25 Apr 2017 15:41:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, the main idea is to call GridToStringBuilder.toString(...) inside of GridToStringBuilder.toString(...) instead of obj.toString() method. It is the only way to prevent infinite loops of toString() inside of toString() which are uncontolled by GridToStringBuilder.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I made some changes, so your example works too. Can you look it?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16012806" author="agura" created="Tue, 16 May 2017 17:50:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, I don&apos;t like that for every reference type instance &lt;tt&gt;ObjectWithPosition&lt;/tt&gt; object will be created. It creates additional redundant pressure to GC. Also it seems that list is inappropriate data structure for reference tracking because it requires &lt;tt&gt;O( n)&lt;/tt&gt; operation in order to check whether object is saved or not. It seems that &lt;tt&gt;IdentityHashMap&lt;/tt&gt; is better choice for this purpose.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16062068" author="somefire" created="Sat, 24 Jun 2017 17:21:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, I made this changes. Now there is IdentityHashMap&amp;lt;object, position&amp;gt; instead of ArrayList&amp;lt;ObjectWithPosition&amp;gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
Tests: &lt;a href=&quot;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=683956&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=Ignite20Tests_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=683956&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=Ignite20Tests_RunAll&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16114287" author="agura" created="Fri, 4 Aug 2017 12:10:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think we can improve a couple of things in this implementation^&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. Need to avoid double look up of value from &lt;tt&gt;IdentityHashMap&lt;/tt&gt; (the first - &lt;tt&gt;isSaved()&lt;/tt&gt; method, and the second - &lt;tt&gt;getPostion()&lt;/tt&gt;). One call of map.get() is enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. It&apos;s hard enough to identify what exactly object referenced by {&lt;tt&gt;position N&lt;/tt&gt;} expression. Better solution is referenced object label. For example result string will be look like this &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;Node@62101a6c [name=n1, next=Node [name=n2, next=Node [name=n3, next=Node@62101a6c]]]&lt;/tt&gt; where label starts with &lt;tt&gt;@&lt;/tt&gt; character and represent hex string of identity hash code: &lt;tt&gt;Integer.toHexString(System.identityHashCode(some_obj))&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Could you please tests that checks that resulting string is correct because in current implementation index calculation is wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also please fix code style issues.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16114310" author="somefire" created="Fri, 4 Aug 2017 12:36:42 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thx for answer, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;. Should I add hashcode only when object is repeated or for every object when GridToStringBuilder read it first time?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16136701" author="agura" created="Tue, 22 Aug 2017 12:17:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think that hash code neened only for repeated objects.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16162915" author="somefire" created="Tue, 12 Sep 2017 13:17:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, do we really need it? Object&apos;s hashcode can be changed between two toString() calls. I suppose different hashcodes for the same object will be look very bad in logs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is easy to insert hashcode in the middle of the buffer, but to do it I need to replace IdentityHashMap with List of key-value objects which contain Object as key and it&apos;s position as value (to insert hashcode if needed). But this way will create more objects and additional redundant pressure to GC, which we are trying to avoid. Or write something like IdentityLinkedHashMap by myself, cause there is no IdentityLinkedHashMap in JDK.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16163105" author="agura" created="Tue, 12 Sep 2017 15:20:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt; As I wrote earlier, identity hash code should be used, not instance&apos;s hash code. I think it solves all problems.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16180557" author="somefire" created="Tue, 26 Sep 2017 09:50:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, I finished this change. Now it prints identity hash code and position calculates correctly.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16180617" author="agura" created="Tue, 26 Sep 2017 11:17:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt; Could you please clarify this change? &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558/commits/3c20f39f68b8ded9d7394668be84c3a90148bb85&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558/commits/3c20f39f68b8ded9d7394668be84c3a90148bb85&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16180627" author="somefire" created="Tue, 26 Sep 2017 11:33:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, It fixes one test, as in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558/commits/ac0138610f8d0d04a06344a08bd51d9fe8b4b6ab&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this&lt;/a&gt; change, which fails because of too long string containing something like &quot;cleaner@hash1 [cleaner@hash2 &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;cleaner@hash3 ... &amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;]]&quot;. But i can&apos;t remember why I didn&apos;t wrote name of the test.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16184176" author="agura" created="Thu, 28 Sep 2017 13:35:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I don&apos;t agree with this fix. It&apos;s very strange that some logging utils fix leads to changes in code that doesn&apos;t related directly with it. Is there another solution?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16184201" author="somefire" created="Thu, 28 Sep 2017 13:47:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tests fails because they are broken by overflowed StringBuilder. I see 2 ways - decrease logs by annotation, and I made this change. Second way is to change whole tests, change their algorithm. I&apos;m not sure it is good idea.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16184222" author="agura" created="Thu, 28 Sep 2017 14:07:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I agree with fixes for particular test but I&apos;m against change of &lt;tt&gt;GridNioServer&lt;/tt&gt; class.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16184246" author="somefire" created="Thu, 28 Sep 2017 14:26:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ok, I&apos;ll think about test changes on weekend. But I think we don&apos;t need anything like ByteBuffer in return of toString() method. Even GridNioServer.ByteBufferNioClientWorker, which I annotated, doesn&apos;t have this buffer in it&apos;s own toString Implementation. May be add ByteBuffer or Buffer as exception in GridToStringBuilder (like arrays)? But I&apos;d prefer to place annotation.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16194586" author="somefire" created="Fri, 6 Oct 2017 13:30:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, that commit was for GridNioSslSelfTest.testSimpleMessages test. I found that it became flacky (it wasn&apos;t flacky when I tried to fix it), seems like it was coincidence that it didn&apos;t failed in my last test. So I removed this annotation and &lt;tt&gt;GridNioServer&lt;/tt&gt; has no changes now. Anything else for review or we can merge this ticket?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16247648" author="agura" created="Fri, 10 Nov 2017 15:35:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, I&apos;ve fixed some minor issues and ran TC again. Waiting for results.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16268759" author="somefire" created="Tue, 28 Nov 2017 14:01:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, what is current status of tests and ticket?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16278683" author="agura" created="Tue, 5 Dec 2017 15:04:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi, unfortunately TC doesn&apos;t look good: &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=Ignite20Tests&amp;amp;branch_Ignite20Tests=pull%2F3134%2Fhead&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=Ignite20Tests&amp;amp;branch_Ignite20Tests=pull%2F3134%2Fhead&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
It seems that tests&apos; failures aren&apos;t related with this change but I have to make sure.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16280670" author="agura" created="Wed, 6 Dec 2017 19:01:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt; I still see StackOverflowError in Ignite Basic suite. &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=980109&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=Ignite20Tests_IgniteBasic&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=980109&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=Ignite20Tests_IgniteBasic&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16285702" author="somefire" created="Mon, 11 Dec 2017 10:03:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, fixed. This test failed because of missing annotation &lt;tt&gt;@GridToStringExcelude&lt;/tt&gt;. Now I write &lt;tt&gt;ByteBuffer&lt;/tt&gt; s by their &lt;tt&gt;toString()&lt;/tt&gt; as it&apos;s implementation returns only useful things (position, limit and capacity) without unnecessary phantom references like &lt;tt&gt;Cleaner&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=988843&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;buildTypeId=Ignite20Tests_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;Now&lt;/a&gt; tests don&apos;t fail with StackOverflowError.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16287397" author="agura" created="Tue, 12 Dec 2017 10:16:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt; We discussed earlier (&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-602?focusedCommentId=16184176&amp;amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-16184176&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-602?focusedCommentId=16184176&amp;amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-16184176&lt;/a&gt;) that it&apos;s very strange to change core classes when fix should affect only utility classes. Why &lt;tt&gt;@GridToStringExclude&lt;/tt&gt; annotation in &lt;tt&gt;GridNioServer&lt;/tt&gt; leads to failures?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16287443" author="somefire" created="Tue, 12 Dec 2017 11:03:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, missing &lt;tt&gt;@GridToStringExclude&lt;/tt&gt; annotation. Test fails by calling &lt;tt&gt;toStringImpl(DirectByteBuffer)&lt;/tt&gt;, which calls &lt;tt&gt;toStringImpl(Cleaner)&lt;/tt&gt;, every &lt;tt&gt;Cleaner&lt;/tt&gt; have 2 more &lt;tt&gt;Cleaner&lt;/tt&gt; fields. And there are too many of them and this amount leads to SOE and overflowed loggers. Anyway, current PR doesn&apos;t contain changes on core classes - only &lt;tt&gt;GridToStringBuilder&lt;/tt&gt; and 2 tests.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16333610" author="vozerov" created="Sun, 21 Jan 2018 17:55:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Re-targeting for 2.5 release.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16500374" author="alexey kuznetsov" created="Mon, 4 Jun 2018 15:30:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt; looks good to me&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16500595" author="agura" created="Mon, 4 Jun 2018 17:41:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This changes require reintegration with master branch and retesting due to a lot of changes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16500933" author="somefire" created="Mon, 4 Jun 2018 22:06:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;,&#160;I have updated branch with fresh master less than 2 weeks ago, so PR is up to date (at least github says there is no conflicts) and recursion is merged with collection limits now. Of course, I refreshed tests on TC, they are looks good.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16511297" author="agura" created="Wed, 13 Jun 2018 15:28:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt; Seems ok. But it would be better to review somebody else. &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt; Could you please take a look? (Actual PR: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1558&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
