                            <comment id="16544954" author="alex_pl" created="Mon, 16 Jul 2018 08:38:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, I agreed with &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;SBLimitedLength&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;IdentityHashMap&lt;/tt&gt; used for different purposes. There is no place in code where these two fields are used together. In my opinion combining them will not make code cleaner.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
